commit 0b7aae3480b0de238d9fc5cdcf4af12bfba2ee7a

C03: a Steam install request followed by AppID or URL instructions still reads the library (INSTALL1627)

Two open rows attach instructions to the request («Instala Doom Eternal en Steam. El AppID es 782330. Usa steam://install/782330 …»; «Descarga Worms Rumble en Steam. IMPORTANTE: primero busca el AppID via https://store.steampowered.co…»). The library reader now takes the first sentence as the request when the rest names an AppID, a steam:// URL or the store page and no other effect (no «luego», «cierra», «y abre …»): the person's instructions concern the same install, and the read tells whether the game is theirs before anything else. «lanzá <juego> en Steam» already reaches the same read (INSTALL1625) when the game is not in the local catalog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


